/**
 * Every option, setting and tool BeeZilla has, in one list: the data behind "All options"
 * (/buzzy/options). A tester's words: "the options are everywhere… have a page where all
 * options and settings are displayed, if I can't find something." Plain data:
 * window.BZ_OPTIONS.
 *
 * One object per option:
 *   group  the place it is used (the headings on the page, in this order)
 *   name   the option as the page shows it
 *   what   one plain line on what it does
 *   where  how to reach it, step by step
 *   href   the page to open (no #hash: no page reacts to one)
 *   words  other words people use for it, so a search finds it ("stretch", "resolution"…)
 *   src    where it comes from: "<file>|<exact words in it>". The page never shows it;
 *          scripts/test-options-data.mjs fails if those words leave that file (a path
 *          starting src/ or scripts/ is from the repo root, anything else is public/buzzy/),
 *          so a button that is renamed or removed cannot stay on this page.
 *
 * Only what the code has today. When a control is added, renamed or removed, change its
 * line here in the same commit. Left out on purpose: controls nothing shows (the parked
 * Mode tabs and Conversations drawer in talk.html), and /buzzy/remember, which no page
 * links to.
 */
